{
  "chosen": "Add early evasion when any mover is within a danger distance, because side/back movers caused collisions that the front‑gap check missed",
  "target": "_DANGER_DIST constant, _danger_close function, controller logic",
  "direction": "1. Define a new constant `_DANGER_DIST = 2.0` near the other safety constants. 2. Add a helper `def _danger_close(pose, movers):` that iterates over `movers` and returns True if `math.hypot(mx - pose[0], my - pose[1]) < _DANGER_DIST`. 3. In `controller()`, after `movers = _movers(t, pose)` and before computing `gap = _front_gap(pose)`, insert `if _danger_close(pose, movers): v,w = _evade(pose, movers, target, False); return v,w,False`. 4. Keep the existing `gap`‑based stop/detour logic unchanged for forward obstacles. 5. Place the new function after `_movers` (or any other helper) so it is available to the controller. 6. No other code changes are required."
}
